  <prompt>
    Scaffold a new shared package under `src/client/shared/` for the LegalWorkspace section registry. Mirror the structure of `Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components` (closest structural analogue). Create package.json (name TBD — recommend `@spaarke/legal-workspace`), tsconfig.json, src/index.ts, and a build step that publishes types. Do NOT migrate content yet — task 021 handles migration.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer scaffolding a new npm package under monorepo conventions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    New shared package exists under `src/client/shared/{PackageName}/`. Independent build succeeds. Types emit correctly. Package is discoverable by npm workspace / monorepo tooling. No content migrated yet (task 021).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      SpaarkeAi's `vite.config.ts` aliases `@spaarke/legal-workspace` to `../LegalWorkspace/src` — a source alias, not an npm dependency. This causes the dual-deploy trap: LegalWorkspace deploys don't reach SpaarkeAi unless SpaarkeAi is also rebuilt. FR-10 (adopted 2026-07-02 per owner clarification) eliminates the trap by extracting the section registry into a proper shared package.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/{new-package}/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">New shared library follows SSOT rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Package stays React-16-safe (may need React-16-compat if section registry is consumed by any PCF surface — verify during task 021 migration).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§11">Component Justification — see justification block below.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Package name: recommend `@spaarke/legal-workspace`; final name confirmed during scaffolding per Spaarke conventions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Package structure mirrors `Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components` (closest structural analogue).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>`src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/` is closest structural analogue (domain-specific section registry + widgets). No overlap in scope — DailyBriefing is briefing-specific; new package is LegalWorkspace-scope.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot extend `Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components` — different domain (daily briefing vs LegalWorkspace section registry). Could theoretically inline the section registry in `Spaarke.UI.Components` but that violates ADR-012 SSOT: LegalWorkspace-specific code shouldn't live in the shared UI-components library.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The SpaarkeAi ← LegalWorkspace source-alias trap continues. Every future section-registration edit requires dual-rebuild coordination. New team members debug the trap for 30+ min per encounter (documented in design.md § Issue 12 — actual 2026-07-01 incident). Concrete failure = onboarding friction + deploy drift.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

